by GromNaN at 2026-10-12T13:03:11Z

Thanks for the review, both points are addressed.

The generated normalization is removed. The method is descriptive again, and the rewriting stays
in the `beforeNormalization()` closure of the bundle, which is the one that knows how to name the
element. The definition now fails fast when the parent node has no such closure.

The keys that stay in the parent are no longer a list to maintain. The key that names the
elements, the one of `useAttributeAsKey()`, is left out of the shape given at the parent level.
A key declared by both the parent and the elements is rejected at definition time, so the schema
and the closure cannot drift apart on the keys that the parent keeps.

For `doctrine.dbal`, the flat branch is the 3 keys of the section plus the 46 options of a
connection, and `name` is not one of them.

